# A `word-chars` class with some but not all bytes from 0x80 has no editor
# form: those bytes are parts of UTF-8 characters.
# error: this pattern has no editor form: it matches a class that holds some but not all bytes from 0x80
@lexer
tokens
    word, eof, err
[a-z]+ → word
'\n' → skip, skip
. → err
@parser
@highlight
    language "T"
    scope-name source.t
    extensions t
    word-chars [a-z\x80-\x9f]
    keyword "if"
list! = WORD*
